STATEN ISLAND, N.Y. -- Just like grabbing a snack from a vending machine when you're hungry, next time you have a headache you may be able to get Advil there too.
That's because the retail division of CVS Health (NYSE: CVS) is introducing automated retail vending machines stocked with on-the-go necessities -- including over-the-counter health products, "better-for-you" snacks and popular personal care products typically sold at CVS Pharmacy locations nationwide.
